{
  "$defs": {
    "BinaryOp": {
      "enum": [
        "Add",
        "Sub",
        "Mul",
        "Div",
        "Mod",
        "Eq",
        "Ne",
        "Lt",
        "Lte",
        "Gt",
        "Gte",
        "And",
        "Or"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "CompatibilityPosture": {
      "description": "Compatibility posture (LLP 0081 §6). The default is `successor-only`.",
      "enum": [
        "successor-only",
        "dual-compatible",
        "predeploy-compatible"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "FieldType": {
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "enum": [
            "String",
            "Boolean",
            "Integer",
            "Real",
            "Json"
          ],
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "`v.vector(dimensions)` — fixed-size admitted binary64 components.\n\n@ref LLP 0132#vector-values-and-declarations — the schema carries the\nfixed dimension so every write and query can enforce one value domain.",
          "properties": {
            "Vector": {
              "properties": {
                "dimensions": {
                  "format": "uint32",
                  "minimum": 0,
                  "type": "integer"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "dimensions"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "Vector"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "const": "Principal",
          "description": "`v.principal()` — nominal typing over the auth-principal id string space\n(the same space as `ctx.auth.userId`, including LLP 0055 agent\nprincipals). It stores and compares exactly like [`FieldType::String`];\nthe distinct variant lets the schema surface *name* an axis as a\nprincipal reference. It is validated by **shape**, never by a\nforeign-key existence check, because memberships may outlive a\nprincipal's deactivation and LLP 0055 recovery preserves the id.\n\n@ref LLP 0056#declaring-a-membership-table — `v.principal()` is nominal\n  typing over the principal-id string space, not an existence check.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "`v.id(\"table\")` — a nominal application-table id. The value remains a\nstring on SQLite and the public wire, while the target table travels in\nthe manifest so membership resource bindings and helper arguments can\nbe checked rather than inferred from a bare string.\n\n@ref LLP 0056#rule-helpers — resource references must name the same\n  declared resource type; a plain string cannot prove that equality.",
          "properties": {
            "Id": {
              "properties": {
                "table": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "table"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "Id"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "Framework-owned relation-incarnation stamp. It is stored as a string,\nbut unlike an application string it is never writable by application\narguments. The paired required foreign-key field is the complete\nrelationship declaration.\n\n@ref LLP 0110#protected-relation-incarnation-and-stamping — central\n  writers overwrite the stamp from the active parent registry.",
          "properties": {
            "RelationIncarnation": {
              "properties": {
                "foreignKeyField": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "parentTable": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "foreignKeyField",
                "parentTable"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "RelationIncarnation"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "`v.assetRef({ upload? })` — a typed asset reference (LLP 0044 §Typed\nreferences; LLP 0007 dated amendment 2026-07-31). Stored as the opaque\nasset id string; the commit boundary validates every write's\nadmission, so a raw string assignment fails there rather than by\nshape. The optional `upload` restriction names the upload-intent\nbinding whose assets the field admits and is what lets write paths\nwithout handler execution derive a commit-boundary admission.",
          "properties": {
            "AssetRef": {
              "properties": {
                "upload": {
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "null"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "type": "object"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "AssetRef"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      ]
    },
    "MembershipPredicate": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A declaration-bound membership semi-join: the structured-filter IR node the\n`eventMembers.memberOf(resourceRef)` / `eventMembers.hasRole(resourceRef,\n…)` rule helpers lower to. There is deliberately **no** global\n`memberOf`/`hasRole` resolver — two declarations can target the same\nresource type, and that ambiguity is an authorization bug factory\n(LLP 0056 §Rule helpers), so every predicate names its declaration.\n\nSemantics: the predicate holds for the effective principal iff a membership\nrow exists in the bound declaration whose `principal` axis is that\nprincipal, whose `resource` axis equals the resolved `resource` reference,\nand whose `role` is one of the effective roles. A null effective principal\n(unauthenticated) matches no rows — fail-closed.\n\nThe node is **authoritative-only**: it is evaluated by a non-recursive\nstorage semi-join that deliberately bypasses the membership table's own\nrow-visibility rules (a locked-down roster must not break role evaluation\nfor guests), never by the pure/optimistic `ValueExpr` evaluator — which has\nno storage and no business consulting membership facts.\n\n@ref LLP 0056#rule-helpers — declaration-bound; `memberOf` excludes\n  `pendingRoles`; `hasRole` names roles explicitly; `resourceRef` is a row\n  field of the queried table or a query argument of the declared resource\n  type.\n@ref LLP 0053#agent-auth-protected-query-inputs-amended-2026-07-14-eng-24906 —\n  admitted `DatabaseCaptured` declarative expression kind, snapshot-bound,\n  with the pinned empty-result capture.",
      "properties": {
        "declaration": {
          "description": "The stable declaration id this predicate binds to\n(`MembershipManifest::effective_id`).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "resource": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/MembershipResourceRef",
          "description": "Where the `resource` axis value is read from."
        },
        "roles": {
          "description": "The satisfying roles. `None` is `memberOf` — every **non-pending** role\nof the declaration. `Some(list)` is `hasRole` with exactly the named\nroles (which may name pending roles explicitly).",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": [
            "array",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "declaration",
        "resource"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "MembershipResourceRef": {
      "description": "Where a [`MembershipPredicate`] reads its `resource` axis value from. Both\nforms are analyzable at subscribe time; anything else — a computed\nexpression, a different resource type, a join through a third table — is a\nload-time error (LLP 0056 §Rule helpers).\n\n@ref LLP 0056#rule-helpers — the two analyzable resource-reference forms.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "A column of the queried (primary) table whose type is the declared\nresource reference. The per-row semi-join; v1 captures a **conservative\ntable-level** dependency for it (coarse wake = re-query cost; the\nreverse choice would be a correctness loss).",
          "properties": {
            "rowField": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "rowField"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "A query argument (dotted path) of the declared resource type. The\nresource is fixed for the whole query, so v1 captures the fine-grained\n`(principal, resource)` index-range dependency, including the\nempty-result form.",
          "properties": {
            "arg": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "path": {
                  "description": "Dotted query-argument path evaluated at invocation time.",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "resourceTable": {
                  "description": "Nominal resource type proven by codegen. Resource-scoped\ndeclarations require their exact `resourceTable`; app-scoped\ndeclarations require `null` and the closed synthetic path. Carrying\nthis provenance in the installed artifact keeps a hand-written\nmanifest from silently degrading an `Id<table>` to a bare string.",
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "null"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "path"
              ],
              "type": "object"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "arg"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        }
      ]
    },
    "MigrationBackupRequirement": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "checkpointLabel": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "rehearsalRequired": {
          "description": "LLP 0081 §7: the target profile names when a restore-derived\nrehearsal must precede production apply. Stamped by preview from\nprofile policy into the canonical body, so the approver reviewed\nthe requirement. Skip-if-false keeps pre-rehearsal plan digests\nbyte-identical.",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "required": {
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "required"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
